    {
      "id": "A5",
      "claim": "a message polled by the wrong recipient stays queued for its real recipient",
      "passed": false,
      "detail": "receive_message() dequeues before checking the recipient and discards the message when it does not match, so a single wrong poll destroys it. Not reached in production, which is why it never surfaced: the orchestrator uses the protocol as an audit log and never dequeues.",
